    [BugFix][CI] Fix cross-runner csrc L1 cache transport (#18123)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fix cross-runner L1 snapshot reuse by giving every producer/consumer the
    same workspace-relative transport path: `csrc/build_cache`.
    
    The cache action's storage version includes the **literal path input**,
    in addition to the logical key. Previously the CPU producer saved with
    `/tmp/vllm-ascend-incremental-build-cache`, while consumers restored
    with a runner-specific `runner.temp` path. Otherwise compatible logical
    keys therefore searched different OBS namespaces. The archive also
    records paths relative to `GITHUB_WORKSPACE`, so a shared relative path
    ensures extraction into the consumer's own workspace rather than the
    producer's physical location.
    
    Production evidence:
    - [Producer
    save](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/37869628129/job/113624720466)
    - [Consumer miss with the same compatibility
    prefix](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/37905719842/job/113746143445)
    
    This patch:
    - aligns all current L1 workflow callers on `csrc/build_cache`;
    - preserves the helper-exported **absolute** build-time directory
    instead of overriding it with the relative transport input;
    - documents the transport-path contract and adds regression checks for
    callers and nonfatal transport steps.
    
    No cache-engine/CMake identity, schema (still 4), locks, L0, OBS
    authorization, or ordinary-build fallback changes. Restore/save
    transport errors remain nonfatal. This does not claim every unrelated
    local filesystem/build error is nonfatal.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime API change. CI L1 snapshots use a new path-version namespace.
    Existing snapshots are not migrated, so the first run can be cold;
    subsequently compatible producer/consumer snapshots can be reused across
    different physical runner roots.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Cache-engine, concurrency and restore-helper suite: **95 passed, 2
    skipped**:
      ```bash
      python -m pytest --confcutdir=tests/ut/_tools -q \
        tests/ut/_tools/test_build_cache.py \
        tests/ut/_tools/test_build_cache_concurrency.py \
        tests/ut/_tools/test_prepare_csrc_l1_restore.py
      ```
    - Caller-path regression fails against the old workflows and passes
    after this fix.
    - Full `pre-commit run --all-files`, manual Markdown hook, workflow YAML
    parsing, actionlint and `git diff --check`: PASS.
    - Independent review of the patch and pinned cache action's
    path/version/archive behavior: no new blocking defect found.
    - Isolated transport integration and fault-injection tests: PASS. A
    container producer and independent host consumers used different
    physical workspaces but the same relative transport path. Both
    same-source and compatibility-fallback restores recovered the producer
    snapshot, yielded **3 inner HIT / 0 MISS / 0 BYPASS / lock_timeout=0**,
    and verified restored artifact bytes with the compiler guard never
    invoked. Cold producer: **3 MISS / 3 SAVED**. With an unreachable
    backend, ordinary build and downstream workflow steps still succeeded
    after restore/save connection errors.
    
    These are deterministic compiler-action transport tests, **not a new
    AscendC/NPU hardware matrix or production warm-build result**. Test-only
    instrumentation is excluded from this PR. Actual production native warm
    reuse will be observed after merge.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
